#question(title: [More continuous functions], centered: true)[
  We want to prove the following theorem
  #slide-block(title: [Theorem])[
    IF $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions
     \
    THEN $h(x) = max {f(x), g(x)}$ is also a
    continuous function.
  ]

  You are allowed to use all results that we
  already know. What is the fastest way to
  prove this?

  #v(1fr)

  #emph[Hint:] There is a way to prove this
  quickly without writing any epsilons.

  #v(1fr)
]
